# The elder calls a child over (US-165). `@pair first second` is for two clan members talking to each other: the first speaks first, the second answers,
# and the lines are shown as speech bubbles over their heads. The words after @pair name them like @who does (a name, a role or a kind), and each line
# is said by the speaker with that word. `@bark talk` is the kind of event: talk, quarrel, courtship, sharing or gift.
@bark talk
@pair elder child

=== start
elder: Come here, little one.
child: Yes, elder!
